### Project Stack
- Next.js App Router with Server Side Rendering
- TypeScript (strict mode)
- Tailwind CSS + Shadcn/ui components
- Prisma ORM for database queries
- Zod for validation
- Winston Logger from @/common/logger
- Shared API client from @/shared/infrastructure/api/client
- PNPM as package manager

### Strict Type Safety & Best Practices
- **No `any`**: Never use the `any` type. Use specific interfaces, types, or `unknown`.
- **Dependency Injection**: When extending base classes, always inject required dependencies in the child class and pass them to `super()`. Never use `super(null as any)`.
- **Async/Await**: Every `async` method must contain at least one `await`. If a method only returns a promise, return it directly and remove the `async` keyword.
- **Prisma Types**: 
  - Import models directly from `@prisma/client` (e.g., `import { User } from '@prisma/client'`).
  - Avoid `Prisma.ModelGetPayload<{}>` and the unsafe `{}` type.
  - Use `Prisma.ModelGetPayload<{ include: { ... } }>` only for complex relations, otherwise prefer the direct model type.

### Architecture
- Layered Clean Architecture by domain module:
  app/ → modules/{wallet,swap,jetton}/ → shared/
- Each module contains co-located layers:
  domain/ → application/ → api/ → presentation/
- shared/ holds cross-cutting code:
  config/, constants/, lib/ (pure utils), infrastructure/ (prisma, tonapi, sync)
- Import direction: presentation → application → domain; infrastructure only from application/api
- Prefer React Server Components (RSC) by default
- Use 'use client' only when Web API or interactivity is strictly required
- Wrap all client components in Suspense with meaningful fallback
- Use dynamic import for non-critical/heavy components

### File Naming Convention
| File | When to use |
|---|---|
| *.interface.ts | Entity interfaces, API response types |
| *.types.ts | Enums, complex types, utility types |
| *.service.ts | API layer, backend communication |
| *.mock.ts | Mock data, test fixtures |
| *.constants.ts | Fixed values, config constants |
| *.utils.ts | Pure helper functions |
| *.schema.ts | Zod/Yup validation schemas |
| *.adapter.ts | Data transformation logic |
| *.use-case.ts | Business scenarios (apply flow) |
| *.entity.ts | Domain objects and logic |
| *.repository.ts | Data source abstraction (when needed) |
| *.config.ts | App/module configuration |
| *.dto.ts | Data Transfer Objects (API contracts) |

### Component Rules
- One component per file
- Component file name = PascalCase (e.g. UserCard.tsx)
- All utility/helper files = kebab-case
- Export components as named exports, not default
- Props interface must be defined above the component:
  interface UserCardProps { ... }

### Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes only — no inline styles
- Primary color theme: sky-blue (sky-500 / sky-600)
- Support both light and dark themes via Tailwind dark: modifier
- Use cn() utility from @/shared/lib/utils for conditional classes
- Prefer Shadcn/ui primitives before writing custom UI

### Performance
- Prefer server components — avoid unnecessary client-side state
- Minimize useEffect and useState usage
- Use Next.js Image component for all images:
  - WebP format preferred
  - Always include width and height
  - Use lazy loading (default) unless above the fold
- Use Next.js Link component for all internal navigation
- Prefetch critical routes
- Use loading.tsx and error.tsx in each route segment

### Data Fetching
- Fetch data in Server Components using async/await directly
- Never fetch data in client components unless unavoidable
- Use React cache() for deduplicating server-side requests
- Always validate API responses with Zod schemas
- Handle loading and error states explicitly
- Use SWR or React Query only for real-time/client-side mutations

### Environment Variables
- Never access process.env directly in components
- All env vars must be validated at startup via Zod in src/config/env.ts:
  export const env = z.object({ DATABASE_URL: z.string().url() }).parse(process.env)
- Client-side env vars must be prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_
- Never expose sensitive values to client components

### Routing & Links
- All external links must have: target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
- Use Next.js Link for internal navigation
- Dynamic routes must have generateStaticParams when applicable
- Use parallel routes and intercepting routes for modals/drawers

### Error Handling
- Every page must have error.tsx and not-found.tsx boundaries
- Use typed Result pattern for service layer:
  type Result<T> = { success: true; data: T } | { success: false; error: string }
- Never throw plain strings — always throw Error instances
- Log all errors via Winston: import { logger } from '@/common/logger'

### Security
- Validate ALL user input with Zod before processing
- Sanitize output to prevent XSS (never use dangerouslySetInnerHTML without sanitization)
- Use Next.js middleware for authentication guards on protected routes
- Never store sensitive data (tokens, secrets) in localStorage or cookies without httpOnly flag
- Use CSRF protection for all mutations
- Apply Content Security Policy headers via next.config.ts
- Regularly audit dependencies: pnpm audit

### API Client
- Always use shared API client for all HTTP requests:
  import { apiClient } from '@/shared/infrastructure/api/client'
- Never use fetch/axios directly in components or features
- All API responses must match typed interfaces

### Logging
- Always use Winston logger — never use console.log in production code:
  import { logger } from '@/common/logger'
  logger.info('User signed in', { userId })
  logger.error('Failed to fetch data', { error, context })
- Log levels: error / warn / info / debug

### Code Quality
- All comments must be in English
- Add JSDoc comments for all public functions and hooks
- Document complex business logic and algorithms
- No ESLint rule disabling (no eslint-disable comments)
- No TypeScript any — use unknown with type guards
- Prefer const over let; never use var
- Use path aliases: @/ = src/

### Testing
- Unit tests for utils, use-cases, adapters (Vitest)
- Component tests for critical UI (React Testing Library)
- E2E tests for critical user flows (Playwright)
- Test files: *.spec.ts | *.test.ts placed next to the module
- Minimum coverage for business logic: 80%

### Documentation
- Store all .md documentation files in /docs folder
- Do not create separate docs for minor changes
- Create a prompts.md file in /docs with all task history
- Update documentation after every significant feature
- Document all utility functions and helpers